<body>

  <h1>MINI ERP + CRM OPERATIONS PORTAL</h1>
  <p><strong>Comprehensive Project Architecture, Module Specifications & System Documentation</strong></p>

  <div class="meta-box">
    <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Project Title:</strong> Mini ERP + CRM Operations Portal for Wholesale Distribution</p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0 0 0;"><strong>Developer / Author:</strong> Aritra Banerjee</p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0 0 0;"><strong>GitHub Repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/AritraBanerjee-09/mini-erp-crm">https://github.com/AritraBanerjee-09/mini-erp-crm</a></p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0 0 0;"><strong>Date:</strong> July 2026</p>
  </div>

  <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #CBD5E1; margin: 25px 0;">

  <h2>1. Executive Summary & Business Context</h2>
  <p>
    The <strong>Mini ERP + CRM Operations Portal</strong> is a full-stack, enterprise-grade management application custom-built for wholesale and distribution companies. The system unifies key business operations—customer relationship management (CRM), catalog inventory management, warehouse stock movement auditing, automated sales challan dispatching, tax invoicing, and instant PDF receipt generation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application solves critical challenges faced by wholesale distributors:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Preventing Stock Shortfalls:</strong> Implements real-time stock guards to ensure inventory never drops below zero and automatically alerts warehouse managers when stock reaches minimum thresholds.</li>
    <li><strong>Historical Price Integrity:</strong> Stores immutable snapshots of product details at the exact time of order placement, protecting historical sales challans and tax invoices from future price modifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Role-Based Security:</strong> Restricts operational actions based on user roles (Admin, Sales, Warehouse, Accounts) to prevent unauthorized transactions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. User Roles & Access Control (RBAC)</h2>
  <p>
    The system implements strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) with pre-seeded demo user profiles for instant testing:
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Role</th>
        <th>Pre-seeded Email</th>
        <th>Default Password</th>
        <th>Permissions & Scope</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Admin</strong></td>
        <td><code>admin@minierp.com</code></td>
        <td><code>Password123</code></td>
        <td>Full unrestricted access across all modules (CRM, Inventory, Sales, Billing, and User Management).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Sales Executive</strong></td>
        <td><code>sales@minierp.com</code></td>
        <td><code>Password123</code></td>
        <td>Manage Customer CRM profiles, log follow-up notes, create Draft & Confirmed Sales Challans.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Warehouse Manager</strong></td>
        <td><code>warehouse@minierp.com</code></td>
        <td><code>Password123</code></td>
        <td>Manage product inventory, track low-stock alerts, record manual stock IN/OUT movements, view audit logs.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Accounts Executive</strong></td>
        <td><code>accounts@minierp.com</code></td>
        <td><code>Password123</code></td>
        <td>Review confirmed sales challans, generate official tax invoices, export downloadable PDF tax receipts.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>3. Technology Stack & Architecture</h2>
  
  <h3>Backend Architecture</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Runtime Environment:</strong> Node.js (v18+) with TypeScript for strict type safety.</li>
    <li><strong>Web Framework:</strong> Express.js REST API server with modular routing.</li>
    <li><strong>Database & ORM:</strong> Prisma ORM connected to PostgreSQL / SQLite database engines.</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> JSON Web Tokens (JWT) with 24-hour expiration and bcrypt password hashing.</li>
    <li><strong>Request Validation:</strong> Zod schema validation ensuring strict input sanitization.</li>
    <li><strong>Document Generation:</strong> PDFKit stream generator for vector PDF tax receipts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Frontend Architecture</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>UI Framework:</strong> React 18 with TypeScript and Vite.</li>
    <li><strong>Design System:</strong> Modern dark-mode Glassmorphism design system using CSS tokens (glowing borders, blur filters, status pills).</li>
    <li><strong>Iconography:</strong> Lucide React vector icons.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Core Modules Specification</h2>

  <h3>A. Authentication & Registration Module</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>User Registration:</strong> Allows any user to create an account by providing Full Name, Email, Password, and assigned Role.</li>
    <li><strong>User Login:</strong> Authenticates credentials and returns a signed JWT token.</li>
    <li><strong>Quick Role Switcher:</strong> Provides 1-click quick login demo cards on the login screen for testing permissions without typing credentials.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B. Customer CRM Module</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Profile Fields:</strong> Customer Name, Business Name, Mobile Number, Email, GST Number, Customer Type (Retail, Wholesale, Distributor), Address, Status (Lead, Active, Inactive), Follow-up Date, and Initial Notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Search & Filter:</strong> Real-time search across Name, Business, Mobile, Email, and GST numbers. Filter by Status and Customer Type.</li>
    <li><strong>Follow-up Timeline:</strong> Interactive detail view showing chronological history of follow-up notes with staff attribution and auto-updated next follow-up dates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>C. Product & Inventory Control Module</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Catalog Attributes:</strong> Name, SKU Code, Category, Unit Price, Current Stock, Minimum Stock Alert Threshold, Warehouse Location.</li>
    <li><strong>Low Stock Monitor:</strong> Visual warning badges and dashboard alerts when stock drops below threshold.</li>
    <li><strong>Stock Movement Audit Logs:</strong> Tracks every stock change with quantity changed, movement type (IN/OUT), reason, created by user, and timestamp.</li>
    <li><strong>Manual Stock Adjustments:</strong> Dedicated modal for receiving stock shipments or logging inventory adjustments.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>D. Sales Challan Module</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order Builder:</strong> Select customer and add multiple product line items with real-time stock availability feedback.</li>
    <li><strong>Auto Challan Numbering:</strong> Automatically generates sequential numbers (e.g. <code>CH-202607-0001</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Stock Guard Logic:</strong> Confirming a sales challan atomically reduces stock and logs <code>OUT</code> movement entries. Prevents negative stock with explicit validation errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Product Snapshot Data:</strong> Stores immutable snapshots of product details (name, SKU, unit price) at creation time to protect against price modifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Status Lifecycle:</strong> Draft &rarr; Confirmed (deducts stock) or Confirmed &rarr; Cancelled (restores stock).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>E. Invoices & PDF Export Module</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Invoice Generation:</strong> Generates official tax invoices from confirmed sales challans with a default 30-day payment credit window.</li>
    <li><strong>PDF Receipt Export:</strong> Instant dynamic PDF generation via <code>/api/invoices/:id/pdf</code> formatted with corporate tax headers, itemized breakdown tables, and grand total summaries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. REST API Endpoint Reference</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>HTTP Method</th>
        <th>Endpoint Path</th>
        <th>Description</th>
        <th>Required Role</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/auth/register</code></td><td>Register new user account</td><td>Public</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/auth/login</code></td><td>Authenticate user & get JWT token</td><td>Public</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/auth/me</code></td><td>Fetch current user profile</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/customers</code></td><td>Search & list CRM customers</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/customers</code></td><td>Create new customer profile</td><td>Admin, Sales</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/customers/:id/followups</code></td><td>Add follow-up note to customer</td><td>Admin, Sales</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/products</code></td><td>List inventory items & stock levels</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/products</code></td><td>Add catalog product</td><td>Admin, Warehouse</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/products/stock-movement</code></td><td>Record manual stock IN/OUT</td><td>Admin, Warehouse</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/products/:id/stock-logs</code></td><td>Fetch stock audit history for item</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/challans</code></td><td>List sales challans</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/challans</code></td><td>Create sales challan</td><td>Admin, Sales</td></tr>
      <tr><td>PUT</td><td><code>/api/challans/:id/status</code></td><td>Update challan status (Confirm/Cancel)</td><td>Admin, Sales, Warehouse</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/invoices</code></td><td>List tax invoices</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/invoices/generate/:challanId</code></td><td>Generate tax invoice from challan</td><td>Admin, Accounts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/invoices/:id/pdf</code></td><td>Stream downloadable PDF tax receipt</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/dashboard/stats</code></td><td>Fetch operational dashboard overview</td><td>Authenticated</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>6. How to Run the Project Locally</h2>

  <h3>Backend Setup</h3>
  <div class="code-block">
cd backend
npm install
npx prisma db push
npx prisma db seed
npm run dev
  </div>
  <p>Backend API server runs at <code>http://localhost:5000</code>.</p>

  <h3>Frontend Setup</h3>
  <div class="code-block">
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
  </div>
  <p>Frontend Web Portal runs at <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</p>

  <h2>7. Key Business Assumptions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Zero Negative Stock:</strong> Stock cannot drop below zero. Server-side validation rejects any order exceeding current stock levels.</li>
    <li><strong>Snapshot Immutability:</strong> Historical sales challans preserve exact product snapshots at order creation time.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated Stock Restoration:</strong> Cancelling a confirmed sales challan automatically credits back inventory to the warehouse.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment Credit Window:</strong> Tax invoices default to a 30-day payment due window.</li>
  </ol>

